# Backend Code Review & Improvement Workflow

> **Agentic Workflow** — Automatically detects the backend technology, then drives a full review cycle: code quality, security, performance, proposed fixes, and a senior-developer review report. **The agent never commits code** — all changes are staged for human review.

---

## How to Use This Workflow

In Cursor's Agent chat, reference this rule and specify a path:

```
@tech-codelens review <path>
```

**Example invocations:**
- `@tech-codelens review src/main/java/`
- `@tech-codelens review app/`
- `@tech-codelens review .`

**Optional flags (append to your message):**
| Flag | Effect |
|------|--------|
| `--security-only` | Run Phase 3 only |
| `--performance-only` | Run Phase 4 only |
| `--propose` | Generate proposed fix files in a staging directory (default: analysis + report only) |
| `--severity critical` | Only surface Critical + High findings |
| `--depth deep` | Expand analysis to all transitive dependencies |
| `--report` | Write a `review-report.md` file at the end |

---

## Agent Execution Instructions

When executing this workflow, the agent MUST:

1. Read these instructions fully before starting any phase.
2. **Run Phase 0 first** to auto-detect the technology stack before any analysis.
3. Execute all phases in order unless a `--*-only` flag is present.
4. After each phase, emit a **Phase Summary** block (format defined below).
5. Track all findings in a structured **Finding Registry** (format defined below).
6. **NEVER modify original source files directly.** All proposed changes go into a staging directory (Phase 5).
7. **NEVER commit, push, or merge** any code. All changes are for human review only.
8. Prefer targeted, surgical edits — never rewrite a file wholesale unless critically broken.

---


## Finding Registry Format

Throughout execution, maintain a running list using this format:

```
[SEVERITY] [PHASE] [FILE:LINE] TITLE
  Context: one-line description of what was found
  Risk:    why this matters
  Fix:     concrete recommendation or code snippet
  Status:  OPEN | PROPOSED | ACCEPTED | DEFERRED
```

Severity levels: `CRITICAL` > `HIGH` > `MEDIUM` > `LOW` > `INFO`

---

## Phase Summary Format

After each phase, output:

```
=== PHASE <N> SUMMARY ===
Files scanned: N
Findings: C critical, H high, M medium, L low, I info
Time-sensitive: <list any CRITICAL findings that need immediate attention>
=========================
```

