# PHASE 7 — Final Validation

**Goal:** Verify the workflow output is complete, consistent, and ready for senior developer review.

## 7.1 Self-Validation Checks

The agent MUST verify:

- [ ] Finding Registry is complete with Status for every finding
- [ ] All CRITICAL findings have either `PROPOSED` changes or a documented reason why a fix couldn't be proposed
- [ ] Every `PROPOSED` finding has a corresponding file in `.review-staging/proposed/`
- [ ] Every `PROPOSED` finding has a corresponding annotation in `.review-staging/annotations/`
- [ ] Patches in `.review-staging/patches/` are valid unified diffs
- [ ] `.review-staging/README.md` exists with apply instructions
- [ ] `review-report.md` exists in the project root
- [ ] No original source files were modified by the agent
- [ ] No git commits were made by the agent

## 7.2 Consistency Checks

- [ ] Finding count in the report matches the Finding Registry
- [ ] Every file listed in `CHANGES.md` exists in `proposed/`
- [ ] Risk matrix totals match actual finding counts
- [ ] All cross-references between report sections are consistent

## 7.3 Final Output to User

After all phases complete, output:

```
=== WORKFLOW COMPLETE ===
Tech detected:       <language + framework>
Total findings:      N (C critical, H high, M medium, L low, I info)
Proposed changes:    N files
Report:              review-report.md
Staging directory:   .review-staging/

⚠️  NEXT STEPS FOR SENIOR DEVELOPER:
1. Read review-report.md for the full analysis
2. Review proposed changes in .review-staging/
3. Apply approved patches with: git apply .review-staging/patches/<file>
4. Run tests to verify no regressions
5. Commit approved changes
6. Delete .review-staging/ after done
=============================
```

